I do know is:

There are smoking-prohibitionists who are powerful.

Smoking has a highly statistically significant correlation with lung
cancer.

Countries like France and Japan where smoking is more common than in the
USA have lower rates of lung cancer.

Second-hand smoking has been found harmful in some studies, which finding
has been used in attempts to prohibit smoking outright.

Studies of pipe smoking have concluded that it isn't very harmful because
the smoke isn't inhaled the same way that smokers do from cigarettes - but
they do inhale it the same way that second-hand smokers do.  This suggests
that second-hand smoking isn't very harmful.

Cigarette smoke smells terrible.

