Before being allowed to post to this or any other group, a prospective
poster would have to know basic facts and pass a competency test. For
example, he or she would have to have memorized the List prefixes (this
part would of course be specific to this List...the Extropians list
managers would submit their list-specific  items to the appropriate
authorities for inclusion in the test--this is quite common, as when
psychobabblers submit their items to the Great State of California for
inclusion in the tests to become a "Licensed Therapist.")

Memorizing the 25 recognized List prefixes (META:, POLL:, PLEDGE:, POLI:,
PHIL:, ANARCH:, ANARCHO:, HUMOR:, TECH:, TECHNO:, TECHIC:, PPL:, PPO:,
PPG:, etc.) would be like memorizing the Morse code for an FCC radio
license, and just as useful, too!

An essay part could be used by the Examiners to decide who was Extropian enough.

Sample questions for the test to become a Licensed Extropian:

172. "PPL" stands for:

a. people
